{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.CoordinationSurfaceDeficit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationSurfaceDeficit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.CoordinationSaturation","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Asymptotics"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.perNucleon_tendsto_plateau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.perNucleon_tendsto_plateau","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.lean#L143-L154","doc":"**The limit recovers saturation.** Under the surface law, `B/A → ε·k/2` as `A → ∞`: this\nfile refines `CoordinationSaturation.bounded_degree_saturates` (which is the plateau itself)\nby giving the `A^(−1/3)` approach to it, and does not contradict it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.surfaceToVolume_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.surfaceToVolume_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.lean#L136-L141","doc":"**The surface-to-volume coefficient ratio is scale-free.** `ε` cancels, so\n`a_S/a_V = c·(k−k')/k` is a pure-geometry number, testable against the measured residual\nshape with no scale input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.perNucleon_surfaceLaw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.perNucleon_surfaceLaw","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.lean#L119-L134","doc":"**The SEMF volume-minus-surface shape, exactly.** Under the packing surface law the\nper-nucleon binding is `ε·k/2 − (ε·c·(k−k')/2)·A^(−1/3)` — the volume term and the surface\nterm of the semi-empirical mass formula, with no constant beyond `(ε, k, k', c)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.surfaceCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.surfaceCount","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.lean#L116-L117","doc":"The surface count of a compact 3-D packing, **as a hypothesis**: `A_surf = c·A^(2/3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.perNucleon_lt_plateau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.perNucleon_lt_plateau","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.lean#L101-L112","doc":"**The plateau is approached from below.** If the surface degree is strictly smaller\n(`k' < k`) and the cluster has a boundary (`A_surf > 0`), the per-nucleon binding is strictly\nless than the uniform-degree plateau `ε·k/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.perNucleon_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.perNucleon_split","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.lean#L92-L99","doc":"**Per-nucleon binding splits into a volume term and a boundary deficit.** With one uniform\nper-bond energy `ε`, `B/A = ε·k/2 − (ε(k−k')/2)·(A_surf/A)`. The `A`-dependence of the\ncorrection lives entirely in the surface fraction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.bondCount_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.bondCount_split","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.lean#L85-L90","doc":"**The boundary deficit, exactly.** With `A = A_int + A_surf`, the bond count is the\nuniform-degree count `k·A/2` minus `(k − k')·A_surf/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.bondCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.bondCount","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CoordinationSurfaceDeficit.lean#L80-L83","doc":"Total bond count of a cluster with `A_int` interior nucleons of degree `k` and `A_surf`\nboundary nucleons of degree `k'`, by the handshake lemma. Real-valued so the surface law can\nbe fed in continuously. ","signatureChunk":0}]}